        },
        "description": "The 200 tests that changed most against their own history (before a baseline exists: the 200 slowest), one row per test per server version. The cap keeps the page fast at any fleet size - the full inventory is browsable per test via the timeline drill-down, and everything that regressed is always in the table below regardless of rank.\n\n- recent median: typical duration over the last few days (middle value - one unlucky run does not skew it)\n- last run: most recent run, for reference\n- baseline median: what was typical before that\n- abs / rel change: how much slower (+) or faster (-) vs baseline\n- samples: how many past measurements back the baseline - be skeptical of small ones\n\nREGRESSION requires all three: more than the threshold slower, at least +1 second, and 10+ past measurements.",
